   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Kaplan score report study plan</span></nav><section class="hero w hv"><div><h1>Turn your Kaplan test results into an NCLEX study plan</h1><p class="lead">Upload your Kaplan score report, take a photo of it or type it in. Vexcura matches each weak area to the NCLEX-RN client needs categories and puts a study plan on your worklist.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#progress">Bring your scores</a><a class="btn alt" href="/ati-score-report-study-plan#how">How it works</a></div></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>vexcura.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/os-plan-1600.webp" srcset="/img/os-plan-1000.webp 1000w, /img/os-plan-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1600" height="1000" alt="Your plan is ready: topic drills for anticoagulants, insulin, pain medications and lab values, placed on the student's worklist, with study guides below. Fictional student." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>A plan built from a score report's topics to review. Fictional student.</figcaption></figure></section><div class="w"><style>
.os-steps{counter-reset:os;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:16px 0;display:grid;gap:10px}.os-steps li{counter-increment:os;position:relative;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px 12px 58px;display:grid;gap:2px}
.os-steps li::before{content:counter(os);position:absolute;left:14px;top:12px;width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);font:700 16px/30px var(--fb);text-align:center}.os-steps b{font-size:17.5px}
.os-keep{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,300px),1fr));gap:16px;margin:14px 0}.os-keep>div{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:4px 18px 10px}.os-keep>div:first-child{border-top:4px solid var(--good)}.os-keep>div:last-child{border-top:4px solid var(--accent)}.os-keep li{margin:6px 0}
.os-lv{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,220px),1fr));gap:12px;margin:14px 0}.os-lv>div{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:12px 14px}.os-lv b{display:block;font:400 20px var(--fh);margin-bottom:2px}.os-lv q{font-style:italic}
.os-along{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--gold);padding:14px 18px;margin:16px 0}.os-along p{margin:0}
.os-src{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);padding-left:22px}.os-src li{margin:6px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.os-cite{font-size:.72em;line-height:0}.os-cite a{text-decoration:none}
.os-disc{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px;margin-top:28px}
.os-plan>div{border-radius:8px}.os-tl{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted)}</style><h2>What your Kaplan report tells you</h2><p>Kaplan describes its integrated testing for nursing schools as NCLEX-style assessments with benchmark testing, topic-specific assessments and remediation materials.<sup class="os-cite"><a href="#src-kap" aria-label="Source 1">[1]</a></sup> Schools describe the details in their own policies. Marian University's Kaplan Testing Program Policy, for example, refers to Kaplan Integrated tests, Focus Review tests and a Secure Predictor, and talks about results in terms of percentile ranges and a probability to pass the NCLEX.<sup class="os-cite"><a href="#src-marian" aria-label="Source 2">[2]</a></sup> The tests and terms your program uses may differ.</p>
      <p>In Vexcura you enter the overall result your report shows (a percent, or a probability if it gives one) and the topics or areas it flags.</p>
        <p>Vexcura uses the overall result you enter only to label your record and to judge how much to include. The plan itself comes from the topics or areas your report flags.</p>
        <h2 id="how">How to bring in your Kaplan results</h2><ol class="os-steps"><li><b>Open Bring your scores</b><span>Sign in to Vexcura and choose Bring your scores from My Chart (Summary), Results (Exams) or the Menu.</span></li><li><b>Choose who made the test</b><span>Pick ATI, HESI, Kaplan, UWorld or another test maker. Vexcura only uses the name to label your result.</span></li><li><b>Bring in the report</b><span>Upload your Kaplan score report PDF, take a photo of it, or type the results. A PDF is read in your own browser. A photo stays on your screen beside the form so you can type from it; Vexcura doesn't read text from photos.</span></li><li><b>Check what Vexcura found</b><span>Confirm the test name, date, overall score or proficiency level, and each topic to review. Every topic is matched to a Vexcura study topic under one of the 8 NCLEX-RN client needs categories, and Vexcura asks you to pick when a match is uncertain. Fix anything that's wrong before you save.</span></li><li><b>Get your study plan</b><span>Targeted topic drills, study guides, EHR practice where a topic has a matching clinical activity, and a checkpoint quiz go on your Vexcura worklist, starting today.</span></li><li><b>Add your next score</b><span>When you take the next test, add it the same way. Vexcura shows the new result next to the previous one, along with your practice accuracy in your weak topics.</span></li></ol>
        <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>vexcura.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/os-confirm-1600.webp" srcset="/img/os-confirm-1000.webp 1000w, /img/os-confirm-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1600" height="1000" alt="Bring your scores, step 3 of 4: a fictional student checks the test name, date, a 61% score, Level 1 and four topics to review, each matched to a Vexcura study topic" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Checking a result and its matched topics before saving. Fictional student and test.</figcaption></figure>
        <h2>What your study plan includes</h2><div class="feat os-plan">
     <div><b>Topic drills</b>Up to six drills of 10 questions with rationales, one for each of your weakest topics, spread over the next few days, two a day.</div>
     <div><b>Study guides</b>Up to four of Vexcura's free study guides that match those topics, ready to read online or print.</div>
     <div><b>EHR practice</b>When a weak topic has a matching clinical activity, a practice session in the academic EHR is added.</div>
     <div><b>A checkpoint</b>A quick round at the end of the plan to check where you stand before your next test.</div></div>
    <p>Plan items appear on your worklist and in the Brain sidebar, the same place your instructors' assignments arrive. Start the first drill right away or come back later.</p>
        <h2>What's kept, and what isn't</h2><div class="os-keep">
     <div><h3>What Vexcura keeps</h3><ul>
      <li>Who made the test, the test name and the date you took it</li>
      <li>Your overall score, proficiency level or predicted probability, whichever your report shows</li>
      <li>Topic names, with their scores or a "to review" flag</li>
      <li>The Vexcura study topic each one is matched to, and the plan built from them</li></ul></div>
     <div><h3>What it never takes</h3><ul>
      <li>Your ATI, HESI, Kaplan or UWorld username or password. Vexcura never asks for them, and the server refuses any request that contains login fields.</li>
      <li>Test questions. Only topic names are saved; a topic line that looks like a test question is rejected.</li>
      <li>Your PDF or photo, unless you tick "Keep a copy" (off by default). A kept copy can be opened only by you, and you can remove it.</li>
      <li>Patient identifiers. Entries that look like a medical record number or Social Security number are refused.</li></ul></div></div>
    <h3>Who can see your results</h3>
    <p>You can always see your own results. If you belong to a nursing program in Vexcura, a box on the check screen lets your instructors see a result you add. It's on by default, and you can turn it off before you save or change it later. Results your program imports about you are visible to you and to your program's instructors and program admins. You can edit or delete any result you added; deleting one also removes plan items that haven't reached your worklist yet.</p>
    <h3>Anonymous totals, never individuals</h3>
    <p>Each day Vexcura writes new practice questions. To decide which topics to write about, it looks at an anonymous count of the topics students are commonly weak in. Any topic with fewer than 5 students is left out of that count, so no one's results can be singled out, and no vendor names or report content go into the questions.</p>
        <h2>For instructors</h2><p>Instructors and program admins see an <b>Outside scores</b> tab in the instructor workspace:</p>
    <ul><li><b>Import a cohort.</b> Use the CSV or Excel export from the test maker's site. The file is read in the instructor's browser, and only the matched scores are sent. Rows match your students by email, or by name within your program; rows that don't match are listed with the reason.</li>
     <li><b>See who needs help.</b> Short summaries such as "5 of 8 students below Level 2 in Pharmacology" or "4 of 8 students have Anticoagulants and antiplatelets to review", with the names one tap away.</li>
     <li><b>Assign the remediation.</b> Assign a targeted drill to exactly those students, with a due date. It's on their worklist the next time they open Vexcura.</li>
     <li><b>Keep the record.</b> Download a remediation record as a CSV or print it: each student's outside result, topics to review, the remediation assigned and completed, and their Vexcura practice accuracy in that area.</li></ul>
    <p><a href="/nclex-remediation-for-nursing-programs">See NCLEX remediation for nursing programs</a></p>
        <h2>Works alongside Kaplan, not instead of it</h2><div class="os-along"><p><b>Keep using Kaplan.</b> Vexcura doesn't give, score or replace proctored exams, and it doesn't reproduce or reinterpret any test maker's questions, reports or remediation materials. It takes the topics your own report lists and turns them into practice in Vexcura. Finish whatever remediation your program requires first; Vexcura adds practice on top of it.</p></div><p>Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools. <b>Students and instructors never pay</b>; students get Bring your scores, the full practice exam and everything else through their school. <a href="/for-nursing-schools">Ask your program about Vexcura</a>, or join with your school's code.</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><h3>Which Kaplan tests can I bring in?</h3><p>Any Kaplan result you can see as a report or type in, such as an Integrated test or a predictor. Vexcura saves the test name you enter, the date, the overall result and the topics or areas flagged.</p><h3>Does Vexcura need my Kaplan login?</h3><p>No. Vexcura never asks for your Kaplan username or password, and its server refuses requests that contain login fields. Upload the report, take a photo to type from, or type the results in.</p><h3>Is my report uploaded?</h3><p>No, not unless you tick &quot;Keep a copy&quot;, which is off by default. A PDF is read in your own browser, and only the details you confirm are saved: the test name, date, overall result and topic names with their scores.</p><h3>Does this replace Kaplan or my program's remediation?</h3><p>No. Vexcura doesn't give, score or replace Kaplan exams or materials. Do what your program requires first; Vexcura adds practice on the topics your report lists.</p><h3>How much does it cost?</h3><p>Nothing for students. Vexcura is licensed to nursing schools, and students and instructors use it free through their school.</p></div>
        <h2>Also works with other score reports</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/ati-score-report-study-plan">ATI score reports</a></li><li><a href="/hesi-score-report-study-plan">HESI score reports</a></li><li><a href="/uworld-score-report-study-plan">UWorld self-assessment results</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-remediation-for-nursing-programs">NCLEX remediation for nursing programs</a></li></ul><h2>Keep practicing</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">The full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-practice-questions">Free NCLEX practice questions by client needs category</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/pharmacology">Pharmacology practice questions</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-study-guides">Free printable NCLEX study guides</a></li><li><a href="/for-nursing-schools">Vexcura for nursing schools</a></li></ul><h2 id="sources">Sources</h2><ol class="os-src"><li id="src-kap">Kaplan, <a href="https://kaplan.com/institutions-educators/higher-education/nursing-schools/integrated-testing-nursing" rel="nofollow noopener">Integrated Testing for nursing schools</a> (page © 2026). Checked November 5, 2026.</li><li id="src-marian">Marian University Leighton School of Nursing, <a href="https://marian.edu/school-of-nursing/_assets/_documents/kaplan-testing-program-policy-revised-sp24.pdf" rel="nofollow noopener">Kaplan Testing Program Policy (revised spring 2024)</a> (spring 2024). Checked November 5, 2026.</li></ol><p class="os-disc">Vexcura is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by ATI (Assessment Technologies Institute), Elsevier/HESI, Kaplan or UWorld. All trademarks belong to their owners. Vexcura describes other companies' products only from their public pages and schools' published policies, cited above. It makes no prediction or promise about NCLEX results.</p></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Bring Vexcura to your nursing program</h2><p>1,220 cited NCLEX-RN questions, adaptive practice exams, 8 NGN case studies, an Epic-style academic EHR and a clinical instructor workspace. The school pays; students and instructors are always free, and every plan includes everything. Students: ask your instructor, or join with your school's code.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools">See Vexcura for nursing schools</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
